   "source": [
    "# BB84 Demonstration\n",
    "\n",
    "Note that `B` carriers Alice's signal to Bob and `E` and `F` are Eve's probles. The QBER is the fraction of sifted bits where Alice and Bob disagree.\n",
    "\n",
    "Note that here `X` refers to the diagonal $\\{\\ket{-}, \\ket{+}\\}$ basis and `Z` refers to the rectilinear $\\{\\ket{0}, \\ket{1}\\}$ basis. The measurement meters conventionally measure in the `Z` basis so a `H` gate in front indicates a measurement in the `X` basis as it rotates the coordinates. When looking at the circuit, the relations are helpful where recall the phase factors ($e^{i\\phi}$ are not important for us),\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\begin{aligned}\n",
    "X\\ket{0} &= \\ket{1}, &\n",
    "X\\ket{1} &= \\ket{0},\\\\\n",
    "X\\ket{+} &= \\ket{+}, &\n",
    "X\\ket{-} &= e^{-i\\pi}\\ket{-},\\\\\n",
    "H\\ket{0} &= \\ket{+}, &\n",
    "H\\ket{1} &= \\ket{-},\\\\\n",
    "H\\ket{+} &= \\ket{0}, &\n",
    "H\\ket{-} &= \\ket{1}.\n",
    "\\end{aligned}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "Look at the [this link](https://quantumchannelzoo.org/) for explainations of the quantum channels."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "3b17944c-a94c-41a9-96e8-3d0ef1e8e2f5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "%matplotlib inline"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "6e5211cb-d210-4fa5-b5ed-e1f0b61466d4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import secrets\n",
    "\n",
    "from modules import BB84, FGGNPAttack, CNOTAttack, InterceptResendAttack, UNKNOWN\n",
    "from modules.channels import AmplitudeDamping, DampingDephasing, Depolarizing\n",
    "from modules.utils.probe_noise import ProbeNoise"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "ca86add5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def run(attack, signal_channel=None, sifted_key_index=0, seed=secrets.randbits(128)):\n",
    "    bb84 = BB84(seed=seed, number_bits=48)\n",
    "    sifted_indices = [i for i, match in enumerate(bb84.alice_bases == bb84.bob_bases) if match]\n",
    "    round_index = sifted_indices[sifted_key_index]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    alice, bob = bb84.key_generation(attack=attack, signal_channel=signal_channel, record_rounds=[round_index])\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(\"Alice's sifted key:\", \"\".join(map(str, alice)))\n",
    "    print(\"Bob's sifted key:  \", \"\".join(map(str, bob)))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    if attack is not None:\n",
    "        guesses = bb84.eve_guesses()\n",
    "        print(\"Eve's guesses:     \", \"\".join(map(str, guesses)))\n",
    "    print(f\"QBER: {sum(alice != bob)}/{len(alice)} = {bb84.qber():.1%}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    basis = bb84.alice_bases[round_index]\n",
    "    bb84.display(round_index=round_index, title=f\"Sifted Key Index {sifted_key_index} | Alice & Bob Basis: {basis}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
